# Steps for SQLA Generation

Install and activate the project

```bash
poetry install
poetry env activate
```

```bash
cd migrations

# delete the old revision test
rm versions/revision_test.py

gen-sqla ../src/analysis_api_schema/schema/analysis_api_schema.yaml > schema.py
python sqlalchemygen.py ../src/analysis_api_schema/schema/analysis_api_schema.yaml > schema.py

# On windows, Powershell will save as UTF-16LE 🤮 you can run this, or open and re-save with UTF-8
Get-Content -Path "schema.py" | Set-Content -Path "schema.py" -Encoding UTF8

# generate the migration
alembic revision --autogenerate --rev-id="revision" -m "test"
cd ..
```

# DB Render

npm install -g dbdocs
npm install -g @softwaretechnik/dbml-renderer

dbdocs db2dbml postgres postgresql://developer:developer@localhost:5432/emsl1000soils -o pg.dbml
dbml-renderer -i pg.dbml -o pg.svg

gen-sqltables src/analysis_api_schema/schema/analysis_api_schema.yaml > prog.sql


# LinkML Dumping

```bash
schemauto.exe import-sql postgresql+psycopg2://developer:developer@localhost:5432/emsl1000soils > schema.yml
# On windows, Powershell will save as UTF-16LE 🤮 you can run this, or open and re-save with UTF-8
Get-Content -Path "schema.yml" | Set-Content -Path "schema.yml" -Encoding UTF8
```

> NOTE! Many features of the Postgres DB _like UUID's_ are not captured by schemauto yet. **Don't rely on schemauto alone!**

# Conrad's Development Process (So Far)

Grab some espresso and lightly aged pop music and dive in!

For LinkML I hav eno experience - so my main aim is to start trying to break it (productively)

Start with something like this:

```yml
# headers ommitted ...

imports:
  - linkml:types

classes:
  # metadata is actually first in the hierarchy !
  samplingActivity:
  sampleBase:
  coreSection:
  replicate:
  sample:
  soil_sample:
  processedSample:
```

This actually is valid YAML and therefor valid LinkML, run the SQL generator to verify

```bash
gen-sqltables ./src/analysis_api_schema/schema/monet.yml
```

My main dev loop is now to make a change, Ctrl+~ UP ENT Ctrl+~ over and over to see the impact on classes, slots, and inheritence.

For instance, what's the actual impact of `is_a` ?

```yaml
classes:
  sampleBase:
  sample:
    is_a: sampleBase
```

produces

```sql
CREATE TABLE "sampleBase" (
        id INTEGER NOT NULL,
        PRIMARY KEY (id)
);
CREATE TABLE sample (
        id INTEGER NOT NULL,
        PRIMARY KEY (id)
);
```

doesn't seem to do anything - however adding a slot reveals the behavior

```yml
classes:
  sampleBase:
    slots:
      - example
  sample:
    is_a: sampleBase
slots:
  example:
    required: true
```

```sql
CREATE TABLE "sampleBase" (
        id INTEGER NOT NULL,
        example TEXT NOT NULL,
        PRIMARY KEY (id)
);
CREATE TABLE sample (
        id INTEGER NOT NULL,
        example TEXT NOT NULL,
        PRIMARY KEY (id)
);
```

Notice that there are no foriegn keys, instead we've simplied copied the structure from sampleBase to sample.
This will be more useful for things like the product tables.



Generic single-database configuration.

# Migration Commands

```
Usage: flask db [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...

  Perform database migrations.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  branches   Show current branch points
  current    Display the current revision for each database.
  downgrade  Revert to a previous version
  edit       Edit a revision file
  heads      Show current available heads in the script directory
  history    List changeset scripts in chronological order.
  init       Creates a new migration repository.
  merge      Merge two revisions together, creating a new revision file
  migrate    Autogenerate a new revision file (Alias for 'revision...
  revision   Create a new revision file.
  show       Show the revision denoted by the given symbol.
  stamp      'stamp' the revision table with the given revision; don't...
  upgrade    Upgrade to a later version
```



```bash
flask db migrate -m "Migration Message"

flask db upgrade

flask db downgrade
```

Look for `INFO  [alembic.env] No changes in schema detected.` in case no changes are detected.
No migration file will be generated.

